To address the issue, you can modify the implementation of `toClass(Object[])` to handle `null` elements within the input array. Here are the potential fixes:

```java
public static Class<?>[] toClass(Object[] array) {
    if (array == null) {
        return null;
    }

    Class<?>[] classes = new Class[array.length];
    for (int i = 0; i < array.length; i++) {
        if (array[i] == null) {
            classes[i] = null; // Handle null element appropriately
        } else {
            classes[i] = array[i].getClass();
        }
    }
    return classes;
}
```

